@startuml

title 12. Implementation gap audit and forward plan

hide circle
skinparam linetype ortho

rectangle "Complete enough for current stage" as Complete {
	[01 Core store/user/reference model]
	[02 Catalog, product parameters and pricing path]
	[03 Customers and suppliers]
	[04 Warehouse stock base]
	[05 Sales orders]
	[05.1 Order comments and history]
	[06 Purchases]
	[07 Payments]
	[08 Inventory posting]
	[08.1 Progress/status sync]
	[09 Reservations]
	[10 Production]
	[11 Status history/audit base]
}

rectangle "Forward cleanup tasks" as Forward {
	[12.1 Admin reference and inventory UI]
	[12.2 Lifecycle and delete policy hardening]
	[12.3 Workflow status drift and history completion]
	[12.4 Advanced inventory operations]
}

Complete --> Forward : do not reopen old stages

note right of Complete
  Audit result:

  - The data model and core services for stages 01-11 exist.
  - Current tests cover pricing, payment recalculation, order history,
    purchase transitions, inventory posting, reservations, production,
    status history recorder and selected DB constraints.
  - Stage files 01-11 can remain historical implementation guides.
  - Gaps found during audit should be added as stage 12.x tasks,
    because the project has already progressed to stage 11.
end note

note right of Forward
  Forward-only gaps found:

  1. Some implemented entities do not have admin UI parity yet:
     Currency, Unit, InventoryReason and InventoryDocument show/list.
  2. Delete/archiving policy exists in UML but needs systematic
     service/controller guards and tests.
  3. Some derived status updates still use direct setStatus paths;
     those should be centralized or explicitly recorded.
  4. Transfer, supplier/customer return UI and inventory reason
     workflows remain advanced inventory work.
end note

note bottom
  Verification rule for all 12.x tasks:

  - Do not modify existing migrations that already ran.
  - Add new migrations only for new schema.
  - Keep controllers thin and place business decisions in managers/services.
  - Preserve existing routes/selectors/response shapes unless the task
    explicitly requires a controlled change.
  - Use Docker commands:
    doctrine:schema:validate --skip-sync,
    lint:container,
    lint:twig templates,
    targeted PHPUnit tests.
end note

@enduml
